---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About | Eugene Agyeman"
	description="Eugene Agyeman is a software engineer in London working on real-time backend systems, mostly in Go."
>
	<div class="doc flow">
		<h1>Hey!</h1>

		<p>
			Backend software, mostly in Go, is what I write. The best part is when the volume
			turns out to be ten times what anyone planned for.
		</p>
		<p>
			My day job is the rules side of a real-time alerting product used by around 20,000
			agencies and more than a million people worldwide. Agencies write the rules, events come in, and the system decides whether
			someone needs to know. The whole thing is mine to look after: the data model, the
			evaluation, and the screens our own operators use.
		</p>
		<p>
			Beyond the rules, I've led other projects at Axon: evidence bundles that hold
			up in court, alert dismissals that sync across every device, and a run of smaller
			ones to make the product nicer to use.
		</p>

		<h2>A typical day</h2>
		<p>
			Design takes up a good part of my time: working through the problem and turning
			it into a plan the rest of the team can build from. Then there are reviews, time
			with our product manager on what we build next, and keeping the engineers building it
			unblocked. Code still gets plenty of my time, just rarely in one sitting.
		</p>

		<h2>Outside of that</h2>
		<p>
			Cooking is back on the menu (the pizzas have come out well), and so is running
			(less well). Lots of returning to do at the moment.
		</p>
		<p>
			Music is always on, and there's more returning here too: Backstreet Boys and
			Jodeci are both back in heavy rotation. I've seen Asake live, in a tux.
		</p>
		<p>
			Travel takes me as far as I can get. Given the choice, a new country beats going
			back to an old one.
		</p>
		<p>
			Most of my reading is newsletters and Hacker News, picking out what's worth
			knowing. Books are next, and I'm on the hunt for good ones, fiction and
			non-fiction. Recommendations welcome.
		</p>

		<p class="mt-12">
			That's the person. The work, with the numbers attached, is on the CV.
		</p>
		<p><a href="/cv" class="link bracket">View CV</a></p>
	</div>
</Layout>
